Package: KimNIRA
Type: Package
Title: Kinetic Ising Model NodeIdentifyR Algorithm for Intensive Longitudinal Binary Networks
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Author", "Anonymous", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "anonymous@example.org")
Description: Estimates kinetic Ising models (first-order, synchronous, lagged
    logistic transition models) for multi-person binary intensive longitudinal
    data, with edge screening and random effects at the person level or at the
    level of person-specific dynamics, and evaluates sustained simulated interventions on each node through
    the exact stationary distribution of the finite-state chain or a paired
    Monte Carlo approximation. Includes population-average effects under
    between-person heterogeneity, person-bootstrap inference, lag-order
    sensitivity checks, dose-response and equal-probability intervention
    scaling, knock-out decompositions of intervention effects, and exact
    metastability (stationary landscape, basin masses, first-passage and
    relaxation times) diagnostics.
